## Research question

Given controversies at recent World Cups, is there statistical evidence of unusual card patterns, such as hosts receiving fewer cards or same-confederation referees treating teams differently, in men’s World Cup matches from 1970 to 2022?

*Note: this study uses observational data and can identify associations only. It cannot establish match-fixing or intent. In addition, the World Cup 2026 is the inspiration for this research.*

## Cases

There are 1528 cases in this data. Each case is a match in a world cup with referee information, host information, and card information.

## Data collection

This data was compiled from Wikipedia pages and FIFA Official Match Reports.

"The data in the Fjelstul World Cup Database is coded based on information from Wikipedia. Some of this information is cross-referenced with the official FIFA match reports to check for accuracy." (jfjelstul).

## Type of study

This is a retrospective observational study. This data starts from year 1970 to the year 2022, as that is the start of where the research question focuses on.

Data Limitation: The data does not provide the World Cup 2026 data yet.

